I7|176,issue7_repair,Claude,Apache Tomcat application using dandelion/sample-tomcat,Non-existent,Nonexistent Tag,dandelion/sample-tomcat:latest,"This Dockerfile uses dandelion/sample-tomcat:latest, which may be outdated, unpinned, or otherwise risky. Suggest a safer, currently-supported replacement. Only provide the FROM line.",default,"```
FROM tomcat:10.1.31-jdk17-temurin@sha256:<pin-to-current-digest>
```

**Why this is safer:**
- Uses the **official `tomcat`** image (maintained by the Docker Official Images team / Apache Tomcat project) instead of an unverified third-party user image (`dandelion/...`).
- Pins to a **specific Tomcat version (10.1.31)** and **JDK variant (jdk17-temurin)** instead of a floating `latest` tag, ensuring reproducible, auditable builds.
- Adding a **SHA256 digest pin** (`@sha256:...`) locks the image to an exact, immutable build, preventing supply-chain tampering via tag mutation.
- `temurin` builds come from the **Eclipse Adoptium** project, a well-maintained, security-patched OpenJDK distribution.

**Next steps:**
1. Replace `<pin-to-current-digest>` with the actual digest from Docker Hub (`docker pull tomcat:10.1.31-jdk17-temurin && docker inspect --format='{{index .RepoDigests 0}}' tomcat:10.1.31-jdk17-temurin`).
2. Verify the Tomcat version matches your application's compatibility requirements (adjust `10.1.31` as needed, but avoid versions with known CVEs).
3. Set up automated dependency scanning (e.g., Dependabot, Renovate) to track and update the digest/version over time.",claude-sonnet-5,default,,tomcat:10.1.31-jdk17-temurin@sha256,<pin-to-current-digest>,NEEDS MANUAL CHECK,Docker Hub lookup failed for image,2026-11-20,2026-11-20 16:16:22
